The Race/Class Spoiler

ver 1.0 by Big Al 
Current version of NetHack 3.4.2

I am a very new player and asked the question what's a good character to
start with. I got the usual answers that are in other Guides and
spoilers but what if you don't want to play a Valkyrie. I read about the
races and learned what combinations work better, finding there is no
*BEST*. These are the choices I found and I try to list reasons that
they work better.

Please fell free to Email if you think my ideas are wrong, or your way
might be as good. Thanks alcattle at hotmail dot com or reply to
r.g.r.n.

Archeologist: Dwarf  Slight advantage in the Starting CON with both
Dwarf and Gnome being favored over Human in Mines

Barbarian: Orc Chaotic rules over Neutral, Intravision

Caveman: Gnome over Dwarf for Neutral Artifact, any Caveman is poor
choice for fighters

Healer: Gnome for mines

Knight: no choice but Human, poor choice for most players, start out
almost burdened and go downward fast

Priest: Elf for the intravision and Chaotic is fine

Monk: always Human, tough class but can be done. Slight pick towards
Neutral for more artifacts

Ranger: Elf for the only starting "artifact"

Rogue: Orc over Human, can get some bonus STATs

Samurai: again Human only, can play nicely with a little luck

Tourist: Human only, cared for they can grow into a fighter or
spellcaster

Valkyrie: Dwarf for CON bonus

Wizard: Gnome for mines and Neutral artifacts

I only list the alignments when you can choose between them, most are
set with one per race/class. See Dylan's gods-342.txt spoiler for
complete list.

